caption: Clergy

Worshipers can be designated as Priests or any variation of that (any Divine class that exists in the setting), but to do so the God must spend 2 character points; one for himself and one for the priest, to establish the Mindlink. Usually, the character must acquire a divine Class themselves, paying the 20 character points to do so. Sometimes Gods do this against the will of the person, usually when they designate them as a champion unwillingly, and usually granting them either the Prophet, Hero or Channel class.

All gods, and some entire pantheons, have a core Vow that is required of all their Clergy. This is sometimes a Code of Honor, but could also be a Sense of Duty, form of Pacifism, or an actual Vow. Additionally, specific classes sometimes have their own Vow requirements, which are also God or pantheon specifics.

All Divine magic for a given God must have the same type of cost: Blood, Fatigue, or Tally. Usually, “Good” aligned gods use Tally, as it is the least personally painful and represents, in the case of divine magic, the degree of favor that the pantheon has for the person doing the casting. Blood is favored by “Evil” aligned pantheons, as that allows blood sacrifice and the creation of magic items quickly through the murder of the church’s enemies. Fatigue is used by older, nature-based pantheons, ones that are frequently seen as morally ambiguous by most.
